   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The Electoral Legislation Amendment (Candidate Eligibility) Bill 2021 amends the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918 to reduce the candidate qualification checklist by six questions and increase transparency by requiring mandatory details on citizenship, birth, and parents/grandparents, with information published on the Australian Electoral Commission website. The bill implements recommendation 1 of the Joint Standing Committee on Electoral Matters' report on the 2019 federal election."
  }
 ],
